From db4036fa6ec7bc561d295d9796f869ebba4bf3c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: auditor <audit@local>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 00:26:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] tools: guard git provenance so measurement reproduces
 on a non-git tree

INVARIANT PROTECTED: a measurement that ran must not be thrown away, and
an outside reviewer must be able to reproduce EDGE.md from the archive as
distributed.

Finding (reported by a collaborating audit, REPRODUCED here 2026-09-05 on
a fresh unzip of `tradingbot_slice76 (2) (1).zip` from
github.com/iceccarelli/ai-agent-control - md5 3f50eea3, byte-identical to
the zip audited in earlier rounds):

    subprocess.CalledProcessError: Command '['git','rev-parse','HEAD']'
    returned non-zero exit status 128

The call sits at the LAST line of `build()`, after every number is
computed. The tool did the entire job and then discarded the result. 51
tools carried the idiom. Practical effect: nobody outside the original
machine could reproduce a single figure in EDGE.md.

Fix: tools/provenance.py returns a sentinel instead of raising.
`UNKNOWN_NOT_A_GIT_REPO` is strictly more informative than a traceback -
it records that provenance was unavailable rather than pretending it was
or losing the measurement. A `-dirty` suffix is appended when the tree has
uncommitted changes, so an artefact cannot claim a clean commit it does
not match. tools/train_policy.py already used the correct guarded form;
that pattern is now the shared helper.

VERIFIED END TO END: a fresh unzip + the patched tool now completes,
exits 0, writes artifacts/slice76_forward_shadow.json with
git_commit = UNKNOWN_NOT_A_GIT_REPO, and reproduces the documented ladder
5/4/0/0/0/0 with constants fingerprint 662de011... intact.

WHAT I DID NOT TOUCH, AND WHY: the first pass rewrote 49 tools and broke
tests/test_slice67_five_day_window.py, which pins the sha256 of the
slice-62..66 apparatus via artifacts/slice67_restored_from_slice66.json.
Those 15 files are DATED RECORDS of what was run at the time. Editing
them - even to fix a real crash - rewrites history, which is the single
thing this programme exists to prevent, so they are reverted and stay
broken on purpose: they are never run to produce new numbers. The
whole-class test exempts exactly those files, and a second test asserts
the exemption stays bounded to slice6[2-6] and fails if the pin manifest
disappears. 35 current-generation tools fixed.

Verification: full suite 5,039 passed, 2 skipped. 6 new tests.
